      "slug": "open",
      "kind": "pipeline",
      "why": "Opening an account is a fixed chain of steps, and each step is one of the safety rules (no secret in the ledger, identity variables removed, key read last), so a pipeline shows the rules in order.",
      "label": "How an account is opened. You pick an account in the tray app or run vvault open. vvault reads the ledger, which holds labels, models and folder paths but no secrets. It removes the environment variables that would override the account's identity, then reads the API key from the OS keychain at the last moment and starts the harness (Claude Code, Codex or Grok) in that account's own home folder.",
